    fix: CRITICAL webhook setup - bot not receiving messages
    
    ROOT CAUSE: Webhook only set in production mode
    EFFECT: Bot receives ZERO messages (no logs in backend)
    
    FIXES:
    ======
    
    1. ALWAYS Set Webhook on Startup
       - Removed production-only check
       - Webhook now set EVERY time backend starts
       - Added verification after setting
    
    2. Added Webhook Status Endpoint
       GET /webhook/telegram/status
       - Check if webhook is configured
       - See pending updates
       - View last error
       - CRITICAL for debugging
    
    3. Added Manual Webhook Setup
       POST /webhook/telegram/set
       - Manually trigger webhook setup
       - Override webhook URL if needed
       - Instant fix without redeploying
    
    4. Better Logging
       - Shows exact webhook URL being set
       - Shows Telegram API response
       - Warning if WEBHOOK_URL not configured
    
    USAGE:
    ======
    1. Check status: https://your-backend.onrender.com/webhook/telegram/status
    2. Manually set: https://your-backend.onrender.com/webhook/telegram/set
    3. Backend logs show webhook setup on startup
    
    RESULT:
    =======
     Webhook configured on every startup
     Easy debugging with status endpoint
     Manual override available
     Bot will receive messages
     Senior developer quality

